.git/
.github/
.venv/
src/
Dockerfile
# The layered images. `Dockerfile` above matches the exact name only, so each
# new one needs saying — and src/web/ui/node_modules is why this matters more
# than it used to: a chart that swept up the source tree would now be hundreds
# of megabytes against etcd's 1MB ceiling.
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
Pipfile
Pipfile.lock
config.json
build.sh
upgrade.sh
*.md
values.local.yaml
cache/
# Locally-seeded historical corpus: gigabytes, and nothing to do with the chart.
matchDetails/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# 1Password reference templates — never part of the packaged chart.
values.local.tpl.yaml

# Everything below is here because the release *secret* has a 1MB ceiling and
# the packaged chart is stored in it gzipped and base64'd — so roughly 700KB of
# chart is already too much. A `helm upgrade` that fails with "Secret ... is
# invalid: data: Too long" is this list being incomplete, not the cluster.
#
# The rule: the chart is templates/ plus values. Nothing that only exists to
# build, test or develop the thing belongs in it.
tests/
scripts/
integration_tests/
.pytest_cache/
.claude/
.vscode/
htmlcov/
coverage.*
*.tgz

# The docs tree. `*.md` above already drops the prose, but not the images that
# prose embeds — and those are PNGs, so the chart's gzip does nothing for them
# and they land in the release secret at close to full size. The banner and the
# three screenshots are ~940KB between them, which is most of the ceiling for
# files no template will ever read.
docs/

# Local caches written by running the code from a checkout. `smite2/` is the
# wiki disk cache and reaches several megabytes on its own, which is enough to
# push the release past the ceiling by itself.
smite2/
session/
matchData/
# The Hi-Rez API dumps the bot caches at its data root, which is the checkout
# when it runs from one. Untracked, regenerated on demand, and 1.4MB and 385KB
# respectively — gods.json alone is larger than everything the chart actually
# needs put together.
gods.json
items.json
rh_capture.json
